\\left(1\\right)+\\left(- 6 e^{2 x}\\right)-\\left(3 e^{2 x}\\right)=1 - 9 e^{2 x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=4 e^{2 x + 2 y} + \\frac{1}{8}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4 e^{2 x + 2 y} + \\frac{9}{8},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(4 e^{2 x + 2 y} + \\frac{9}{8}\\right)-\\left(4 e^{2 x + 2 y} + \\frac{1}{8}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{9}{8}\\right)+\\left(4 e^{2 x + 2 y}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)-\\left(4 e^{2 x + 2 y}\\right)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561534 1080 "I only" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561534 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561534 1083 #uuid "1401c740-8e6c-5777-969c-65265545a041" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561535 1080 "II only" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561535 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561535 1083 #uuid "1a3c83f0-7ed3-51ab-8487-6a57c6adebb4" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561536 1080 "I only" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561536 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561536 1083 #uuid "2a854d42-43c2-553c-8974-9194b1a23ec8" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561537 1080 "II only" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561537 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561537 1083 #uuid "35e79054-058f-5a00-9694-56f64a66fe01" 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561554 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536053 17592186045443 true] [17592186561538 1071 "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by a